### Conditional-update request samples (REST Client / IntelliJ / VS Code format)
### Start the server first: go run ./cmd/server -addr 127.0.0.1:8080
@host = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@resource = demo

### Create -> 201 Created, response carries a strong ETag
POST {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}
Content-Type: text/plain

draft one

### Read -> 200 OK + ETag (copy the ETag value for the requests below)
GET {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}

### Conditional update: replace @etag with the quoted value from GET
# @name update
PUT {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}
If-Match: "v1-REPLACE-WITH-REAL-ETAG"
Content-Type: text/plain

draft two

### Replaying the same ETag after a successful update -> 412
PUT {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}
If-Match: "v1-REPLACE-WITH-REAL-ETAG"
Content-Type: text/plain

late writer

### No precondition at all -> 428 Precondition Required
PUT {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}
Content-Type: text/plain

no precondition

### Weak validator used for a strong comparison -> 412 weak_etag_rejected
PUT {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}
If-Match: W/"v1-REPLACE-WITH-REAL-ETAG"
Content-Type: text/plain

weak try

### Wildcard while the resource exists -> 200
PUT {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}
If-Match: *
Content-Type: text/plain

wildcard write

### Wildcard delete -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}
If-Match: *

### Wildcard update on the now-deleted resource -> 412
PUT {{host}}/resources/{{resource}}
If-Match: *
Content-Type: text/plain

ghost write

### Inspect the in-process fake audit log
GET {{host}}/audit
